title: Free Speech Curtailed
subtitle: Certain "problematic" newspapers are taken over by the state.
view-if: chancellor == "Staal" and (dsu_in_gov or dsu_was_gov) and dsu_policy and ((reichstag_joever_time >= 2 and not staal_post_protests) or (reichstag_joever_time >= 6 and staal_post_protests)) and not staal_rights
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
priority: -1
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/propaganda.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Free Speech Curtailed

In the aftermath of the crackdown against the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, Staal has since moved on to crack down on the free Commonwealth press, which have been dominated by anti-Staal <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span>, <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span>, or the hated Mallin. The chancellor claims that the press is undermining the state and aiding the <span style="color: #700000;">revolutionaries</span> in its biases and fake news.

We know all of this is nonsense, but Staal has slowly taken steps toward the <i>consolidation</i> (synchronization) of his regime, having recently established the "Ministry of National Guidance" in the decree in which he banned the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, to "fight against <span style="color: #700000;">radical Collectivism</span>". 

- @press_censorship

@press_censorship
title: Hopefully nothing happens to The Forward.
on-arrival: {!
Q.press_censorship = 1;
Q.staal_approval += 2;
Q.dufour_staal_r += 1;
if (Q.stampfer_advisor) {
    Q.n_advisors -= 1;
    Q.shuffle_leadership_timer = 0;
}
Q.stampfer_advisor = 0;
Q.stampfer_killed = 1;
Q.pro_republic -= 10;

Q.commons_marcher -= 6;
Q.burgher_marcher -= 4;
Q.guild_marcher -= 2;
Q.landed_marcher -= 2;
Q.faithful_marcher -= 4;
Q.disfavored_marcher -= 4;

if (Q.staal_marcher_r >= 5) {
    Q.commons_marcher += 3;
    Q.burgher_marcher += 2;
    Q.guild_marcher += 1;
    Q.landed_marcher += 1;
    Q.faithful_marcher += 2;
    Q.disfavored_marcher += 2;
}

if (Q.staal_marcher_influence >= 6 && Q.staal_marcher_r < 5) {
    Q.commons_marcher += 2;
    Q.disfavored_marcher += 2;
    Q.left_dissent += 20;
    Q.center_dissent += 10;
    Q.reformist_strength += 5;
    Q.labor_strength += 5;
}

if (!Q.lvp_formed) {
    if (!Q.dstp_gnu) {
        Q.burgher_ddp *= 0.6;
        Q.guild_ddp *= 0.6;
        Q.landed_ddp *= 0.8;
        if (Q.gold_gnu) {
            Q.burgher_gold *= 1.2;
            Q.guild_gold *= 1.2;
            Q.landed_gold *= 1.2;
        }
    }
    if (!Q.gold_gnu) {
        Q.burgher_gold *= 0.6;
        Q.guild_gold *= 0.6;
        Q.landed_gold *= 0.8;
        if (Q.dstp_gnu) {
            Q.burgher_ddp *= 1.2;
            Q.guild_ddp *= 1.2;
            Q.landed_ddp *= 1.2;
        }
    }
}
if (Q.lvp_formed && !Q.lvp_gnu) {
    Q.burgher_lvp *= 0.75;
    Q.guild_lvp *= 0.75;
    Q.landed_lvp *= 0.9;
}
if (!Q.traditionalist_gnu && Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") {
    Q.burgher_traditionalist *= 0.8;
    Q.guild_traditionalist *= 0.8;
    Q.landed_traditionalist *= 0.8;
    Q.faithful_traditionalist *= 0.8;
    if (Q.kvp_formed) {
        Q.burgher_kvp *= 1.2;
        Q.guild_kvp *= 1.2;
        Q.landed_kvp *= 1.2;
        Q.faithful_kvp *= 1.2;
    } else if (!Q.kvp_formed) {
        Q.burgher_other += 6;
        Q.guild_other += 6;
        Q.landed_other += 4;
        Q.faithful_other += 2;
    }
}
if (Q.gnu_formed) {
    Q.commons_gnu += 4;
    Q.burgher_gnu += 8;
    Q.guild_gnu += 8;
    Q.landed_gnu += 4;
    Q.faithful_gnu += 4;
    Q.disfavored_gnu += 4;
} else {
    Q.total_gnu_bonus += 4;
}
!}

With the powers Staal has handed to the new Ministry of National Guidance, fresh directives are now issued to editors, dictating what to print and what to suppress. It is censorship in all but name. Non-compliance brings swift consequences. A realm meant to speak with one voice, the chancellery's men explain, cannot indulge a thousand quarrelling presses.

We have already seen this unfold. The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> has been "acquiring" private newspapers and filling their offices with government loyalists, turning them into little more than state mouthpieces. Many other editors have been forced out of their posts—some for no reason other than being <span style="color: #005EB8;">beast-blooded</span>.

[? if staal_marcher_r >= 5: Staal, however, has been notably lenient with The Forward. Perhaps he is grateful for our past support—or perhaps he is simply waiting until we are too weak to resist. Collaboration, it seems, pays off? ?][? if staal_marcher_influence >= 6 and staal_marcher_r < 5: Using his growing influence over the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, Staal has even managed to install some of his own supporters to quietly "edit" the paper. It's jarring to see our supposed "newfound support" for rearmament—framed as a noble way to provide jobs—splashed across the front page. ?][? if staal_marcher_influence < 6 and staal_marcher_r < 5: It seems even our newspaper, The Forward, hasn't been spared from the crackdown. The offices are raided, staff arrested on dubious charges, and we can't even broadcast the truth for the workers to hear. ?] Stamper hasn't been seen at his desk for some time now. Must be a long vacation.